From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pylibfdt: Fix Python 3 API usage

The fdt_property and fdt_next_node typemaps still use Python 2 C API
names. Python 3 renamed PyString_FromString to PyUnicode_FromString and
PyInt_AsLong to PyLong_AsLong; the old names do not exist in the Python
3 headers. SWIG passes typemap bodies through verbatim, so the generated
libfdt_wrap.c fails to compile with implicit declaration errors.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

---
 scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
index e4659489a96ab1b9c1e0e6e51c0b70fa9cefc888..c738d8056853512fba8745bc07db84c12ebe3508 100644
--- a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
@@ -1033,7 +1033,7 @@
 	PyObject *buff;
 
 	if ($1) {
-		resultobj = PyString_FromString(
+		resultobj = PyUnicode_FromString(
 			fdt_string(fdt1, fdt32_to_cpu($1->nameoff)));
 		buff = PyByteArray_FromStringAndSize(
 			(const char *)($1 + 1), fdt32_to_cpu($1->len));
@@ -1070,7 +1070,7 @@
 
 /* typemaps used for fdt_next_node() */
 %typemap(in, numinputs=1) int *depth (int depth) {
-   depth = (int) PyInt_AsLong($input);
+   depth = (int) PyLong_AsLong($input);
    $1 = &depth;
 }

